  "purpose": "lib/database.types.ts is BYTE-UNCHANGED and these three migrations REQUIRE it to change. Regeneration cannot be run here, and the reason is NOT that the schema is unchanged. This file exists so that a blocked regeneration is not mistaken for a schema that needs no types, and so that whoever runs it can DIFF the result against a list rather than trusting it.",
  "theBlock": {
    "what": "scripts/ci/generate-database-types.mjs and scripts/ci/check-database-types.mjs both call spawnSync without maxBuffer, so Node's 1 MB default aborts both with ENOBUFS on any target whose generated output exceeds it. This project's output is 1,183,384 bytes.",
    "secondBlock": "The only reachable target, SUPABASE_TYPE_SOURCE=linked, is a DIFFERENT DATABASE. It holds 609 relations / 8,020 columns / 151 callables against a 315-migration chain reconstructing 417 relations / 5,363 columns / 224 routines. Regenerating from it would DELETE 78 relations, 112 columns and 27 callables and ADD 285 relations of which 276 no active migration creates. The committed contract has ZERO out-of-band surface against the chain, so it demonstrably did not originate there either.",
    "authority": "CP-089, CP-092. HF-DB-008-REGENERATION-UNREACHABLE-AND-LINKED-TARGET-IS-A-DIFFERENT-DATABASE. CP-016.",
    "owner": "release / ops. The one-line maxBuffer fix is in scripts/ci/**, which CP-112 denies this lane, and the correct TARGET is `local`, which needs a Docker daemon this host does not have."
  },
