  "how_to_verify_a_regeneration": [
    "Diff the regenerated lib/database.types.ts against the committed SHA-256 above. It MUST change, because the contract does not declare any of the objects listed here.",
    "Assert all 8 tables, 4 views and 1 callable appear with the exact column sets above. A regenerated file is DIFFED against this list, not reviewed from scratch - a 25,000-line file cannot be reviewed and a regeneration that silently drops a column is the CP-016 failure this specification exists to prevent.",
    "Assert NO pre-existing relation, column or callable is REMOVED. The database lane's 2026-09-25 measurement established the chain is a strict SUPERSET of the committed contract: 0 out-of-band columns, 0 out-of-band relations, 0 out-of-band callables. A regeneration that deletes anything was taken from the wrong target.",
    "Assert the output is between 1.18 MB and roughly 1.25 MB. Below 1.18 MB means coverage was lost; the ENOBUFS ceiling is 1 MB and a result near it means the fix did not take effect.",
    "Run the scoped typecheck with a program that DOES include lib/database.types.ts, because the default `verify:feature -- --changed` program did not include it on this task (no changed root imports it) and the database lane therefore did not type-check the regenerated contract at all."
  ],
  "what_was_NOT_done_and_why": {
    "regeneration": "Not attempted. The block is real and the target is wrong; attempting it from `--linked` would delete 78 relations and add 285 that no migration creates.",
    "hand_editing_lib_database_types": "Not done. A hand-edit of a 25,000-line generated file is how the file and the database diverge silently, and the generated header would then be a lie. The specification is the alternative: it says what the file must contain so the operator's regeneration is checkable.",
    "escalation": "This artifact IS the escalation. It is filed in docs/engineering/migration-validation/**, which CP-112 grants this lane exclusively, and it is referenced from all three migration manifests and from the task record so that 'regeneration is blocked' can never be read as 'the schema is unchanged'."
  },
